# MODULE 5: BELT RANK, GRADING AND CURRICULUM

Create a complete martial arts progression management system.

### Configurable belt systems

Allow administrators to create custom martial arts ranking structures.

Support:
- Different martial arts disciplines.
- Multiple belt systems.
- Coloured belts.
- Intermediate belts.
- Stripes.
- Dan grades.
- Custom ranks.
- Custom promotion sequences.

Do not hardcode a single martial arts ranking system.

### Belt configuration

Each rank should contain:
- Belt name.
- Belt colour.
- Rank sequence.
- Associated discipline.
- Required minimum training period.
- Minimum attendance.
- Required stripes.
- Required curriculum milestones.
- Grading fee.
- Certificate template.

### Student progression

For every student calculate:

- Current rank.
- Date of last promotion.
- Time at current rank.
- Number of classes attended since promotion.
- Required attendance.
- Required training duration.
- Completed curriculum requirements.
- Outstanding requirements.
- Grading eligibility.

### Grading eligibility engine

Automatically evaluate student eligibility using configurable rules.

Example:

A student becomes eligible when:
- Minimum time at current belt has been completed.
- Required attendance has been achieved.
- Required curriculum has been completed.
- Required instructor approval has been obtained.

Show:
- Eligible.
- Nearly eligible.
- Not eligible.

Display exactly which requirements remain incomplete.

Eligibility does not mean automatic promotion.

### Grading event management

Allow administrators to:
- Create grading events.
- Select eligible students.
- Invite students.
- Register candidates.
- Record examination fees.
- Record attendance.
- Assign examining instructors.
- Record pass/fail results.
- Record grading comments.
- Upload grading documents.

### Promotion workflow

When a student passes:

1. Record the grading result.
2. Update their belt.
3. Record promotion date.
4. Preserve their complete previous belt history.
5. Reset applicable attendance counters.
6. Generate a grading certificate.
7. Notify the student and parent.
8. Update their student profile.

Never delete or overwrite historical belt records.

### Curriculum builder

Allow administrators to define techniques and requirements per belt.

Include:
- Techniques.
- Forms and katas.
- Combinations.
- Fitness requirements.
- Sparring requirements.
- Theory.
- Practical assessment.
- Instructor sign-off.

Allow instructors to record individual student progress.

